rho = k/(1+k) is a defined pulse coefficient: a saturating reparameterization of the raw rate k into [0, 1). The complete update in step 4 is one explicit (forward) Euler step of unit duration of the three mass-action rate equations, all with rate constant rho_ij, with propensities evaluated at the pre-pulse amounts:
- dC_ij/dt = rho(x_i y_j + x_i col_j + y_j row_i);
- dC_mj/dt = -rho x_i C_mj;
- dC_il/dt = -rho y_j C_il.
One unit step of these is exactly the step-4 update.

